From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:48:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/24] media: qcom: camss: csiphy-3ph: leave the PHY in reset
 after a stream

csiphy_lanes_disable() only switches the lanes and the common power-down
off; the PHY itself keeps running. The vendor driver ends every stream by
putting the CSIPHY into software reset. Do the same, and take the PHY out
of reset when the next stream configures its lanes (csiphy_reset() runs
only at power-on, so the release cannot be left to it).

denialwm saw the failure this avoids on Kaanapali: after a D-PHY stream
on one CSIPHY stopped, a stream on another CSIPHY reached the CSID only
about half the time until the camera power domain went down
(linux-perpetua cc2de7a37a7c, written for the phy-qcom-mipi-csi2 driver
of CAMSS v23). This is our own form for the CAMSS v21 CSIPHY code the
Pad 4 runs (front <-> rear switches).

Suggested-by: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Based-on: denialwm/linux-perpetua cc2de7a37a7c (finding; our form for CAMSS v21)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
index dac8d2ecf799..5673fd8e015f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
@@ -1160,6 +1160,9 @@ static void csiphy_lanes_enable(struct csiphy_device *csiphy,
 
 	settle_cnt = csiphy_settle_cnt_calc(link_freq, csiphy->timer_clk_rate);
 
+	/* out of the software reset that csiphy_lanes_disable() left the PHY in */
+	writel(0, csiphy->base + CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
+
 	val = CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRL5_CLK_ENABLE;
 	for (i = 0; i < c->num_data; i++)
 		val |= BIT(c->data[i].pos * 2);
@@ -1201,6 +1204,15 @@ static void csiphy_lanes_disable(struct csiphy_device *csiphy,
 
 	writel_relaxed(0, csiphy->base +
 			  CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 6));
+
+	/*
+	 * Hold the PHY in software reset until its next stream, as the vendor
+	 * driver ends every stream: a CSIPHY left running after a stream stops
+	 * can keep the next stream on another CSIPHY from reaching the CSID
+	 * while the camera power domain stays up.
+	 */
+	writel(0x1, csiphy->base + CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
+	usleep_range(20, 40);
 }
 
 static int csiphy_init(struct csiphy_device *csiphy)
